\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Ah! whither should I go,
\par Burdened, and sick, and faint?
\par To whom should I my troubles show,
\par And pour out my complaint?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. My Saviour bids me come;
\par Ah! Why do I delay?
\par He calls the weary sinner home,
\par And yet from Him I stay.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. What is it keeps me back,
\par From which I cannot part,
\par Which will not let my Saviour take
\par Possession of my heart?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Some cursed thing unkown
\par Must surely lurk within,
\par Some idol, which I will not own,
\par Some secret bosom-sin.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Jesus, the hindrance show,
\par Which I have feared to see;
\par Yet let me now consent to know
\par What keeps me out of Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Searcher of hearts, in mine
\par Thy trying power display;
\par Into its darkest corners shine,
\par And take the veil away.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. I now believe in Thee
\par Compassion reigns alone;
\par According to my faith to me
\par O let it, Lord, be done!
\par                             Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

